# Hygieia — environment variable NAMES only. Never commit values.
#
# Browser (Vite inlines these into the PUBLIC bundle; src/lib/env.ts is the only reader).
# Both unset = LOCAL-ONLY mode: the app runs with no backend and makes no request.
# Set BOTH to enable Supabase: the SHARED Alyssos project (ADR-0003, ref jenbakghoiaiwceyrshz,
# eu-west-1) URL and its ANON (publishable) key. Never the service-role key.
#
# CI (.github/workflows/deploy.yml, PLAN P6.4) reads the six VITE_* names below from GitHub Actions
# repository VARIABLES of the same name (`${{ vars.NAME }}`) for the Pages artifact — variables, not
# secrets, because every value is public by design (it ends up in dist/). The operator sets the
# Supabase pair in OPERATOR-P2 OP2.c and the fleet trio in OPERATOR-P6 OP6.a; until then (and on pull
# requests from forks) they resolve to blanks and the deploy is local-only. CI's e2e and Lighthouse
# builds blank them regardless, so no CI browser ever reaches the live backend.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
#
# Google sign-in flag: set to 1 ONLY after OPERATOR-P2 OP2.a (Google provider enabled on the shared
# project). Off/unset = "Continue with Google" is not rendered; magic-link email sign-in is unaffected.
# VITE_AUTH_GOOGLE=
#
# Fleet telemetry (optional; VITE_FLEET_* is the fleet-wide allow-listed prefix; src/telemetry.ts is
# the only reader). All three set = runtime errors are reported to the fleet dashboard.
# VITE_FLEET_URL=
# VITE_FLEET_KEY=
# VITE_FLEET_PRODUCT_ID=

# Operator-only, shell env for the migration applier (ADR-0003; never in a .env file):
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# HYGIEIA_SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=
